      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "b440a6bb_4fa88076",
      "revId": "049805ea78eec7b51bc08a8079efa92b3d96e3ef",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30aaedb9_2f2e45c9",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/parser/cpdf_parser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 813,
      "author": {
        "id": 9051
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T22:39:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s causing xrefs to be rebuilt, can this potentially cause a performance regression on certain large PDFs that are mostly correct, but have one invalid object? Or are these PDFs already guaranteed to crash?",
      "parentUuid": "99b112ae_f9c6351c",
      "revId": "049805ea78eec7b51bc08a8079efa92b3d96e3ef",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4a99d1e_58cd0c47",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/parser/cpdf_parser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 813,
      "author": {
        "id": 4258968
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T06:02:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my opinion the confusion of where to return true; and where to return false; needs to be addressed. Let\u0027s make it so that return false is in fatal states only and nowhere else (i.e. anything that would have crashed earlier now fails/rebuilds) but everything else stays as is.\n\nIt\u0027s great the CL mostly follows that, but there is one specific place where it is incorrect and fixes the rebuild.\n\nThe place where it is incorrect however is line 962 of cpdf_parser.cpp, and indeed, changing that makes the test work again.\n\nThis means that the rebuild would only happen on PDFs that used to crash before (after the change to 962).",
      "parentUuid": "30aaedb9_2f2e45c9",
      "revId": "049805ea78eec7b51bc08a8079efa92b3d96e3ef",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97b36a07_6de220a1",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/parser/cpdf_parser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 813,
      "author": {
        "id": 4258968
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T06:09:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall there are 2 choices there:\n\nreturn true; - Stop rebuilding xref tables and silently ignore the fact that there is no valid object type. (like before)\nreturn false; - Rebuild xref tables for the case where there is no valid object type.\n\nWould say return true; as it sticks to existing behaviour. If we return true the changes to the unittest need to be reverted. @andyphan@chromium.org @thestig@chromium.org wdyt",
      "parentUuid": "a4a99d1e_58cd0c47",
      "revId": "049805ea78eec7b51bc08a8079efa92b3d96e3ef",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13fa219f_9fc74c69",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/parser/cpdf_parser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 813,
      "author": {
        "id": 4258968
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T06:21:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correction - Not 962 it\u0027s 995 (the section below)\n\n```\n  if (!IsValidObjectNumber(archive_obj_num)) {\n    return false;\n  }\n```\n\nAgain, when this is true (or removed entirely) the table is not rebuilt.\n\nAgain its a question of whether we want to ignore failures or not here. (sorry for the earlier confusion). I\u0027d say we should stay in line with the prior behaviour and return true; here.",
      "parentUuid": "97b36a07_6de220a1",
      "revId": "049805ea78eec7b51bc08a8079efa92b3d96e3ef",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
